  "verbalization": "Prednisone is implicated in the pathogenesis of Allergic Asthma through a series of indirect pathways, all of which involve the treatment of Intrinsic Asthma. The evidence suggests that Prednisone acts as a mediator in the progression of Intrinsic Asthma, which in turn leads to the development of Allergic Asthma. This is supported by the fact that Prednisone is linked to Intrinsic Asthma via three distinct indications: Ibudilast, Reproterol, and Zileuton. Each of these compounds is known to interact with the immune system and airway inflammation, which are key mechanisms in the development of allergic asthma. The shared pathway from Intrinsic Asthma to Allergic Asthma highlights a potential mechanistic link, where Prednisone may influence the inflammatory response in the airways, potentially modulating the transition from intrinsic asthma to allergic asthma. The consistent scores across the three paths suggest a robust, albeit indirect, relationship, emphasizing the role of Intrinsic Asthma as a critical intermediate step in the repurposing of Prednisone for the treatment of allergic asthma.",
